1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:02,570
A mother told me about a day she will never forget.

2
00:00:02,660 --> 00:00:09,130
She was visiting some people, and as she got up to leave, a quick thought crossed her heart:

3
00:00:09,220 --> 00:00:11,540
“I fear my child may be struck by the evil eye.”

4
00:00:11,630 --> 00:00:18,310
She left and got into the car, and within minutes the little one vomited twice in a row.

5
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:21,570
And from that day on... everything changed.

6
00:00:21,660 --> 00:00:24,780
Crying that would not settle, no sleep by day or by night,

7
00:00:24,870 --> 00:00:26,630
for five or six months,

8
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:29,360
and nothing they tried made any difference.

9
00:00:29,450 --> 00:00:38,100
Then we began sharʿī ruqyah with him, and advised his mother to make much istighfar and to recite over him morning and evening,

10
00:00:38,190 --> 00:00:40,320
and healing is in Allah’s hand alone.

11
00:00:40,410 --> 00:00:43,030
Perhaps you, too, have been through something like it?

12
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:52,580
In this episode we look at what the Qur’an and Sunnah say about the evil eye that strikes little ones, and how to treat it and protect our children in the lawful way,

13
00:00:52,670 --> 00:00:57,860
and at the end, a complete daily plan you can start tonight.

14
00:00:57,950 --> 00:01:00,340
The evil eye... reality or illusion?

15
00:01:00,430 --> 00:01:03,830
The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: “The evil eye is real.”

16
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:09,670
In another report: “The evil eye is real, and if anything could outrun destiny, the eye would.”

17
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:18,030
Many commentators mention that the words of Allah, “And those who disbelieve would almost make you slip with their eyes,” were revealed about the evil eye.

18
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:22,800
But always remember: the eye only affects by Allah’s permission.

19
00:01:22,890 --> 00:01:28,410
No one’s glance has independent power, and we are not unprotected, for Allah is the Protector.

20
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:31,620
And why are children affected faster than others?

21
00:01:31,710 --> 00:01:36,210
Asmāʾ bint ʿUmays came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said:

22
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:41,600
“O Messenger of Allah, the eye is quick to reach Jaʿfar’s children. Shall I seek ruqyah for them?”

23
00:01:41,690 --> 00:01:46,880
He said: “Yes, for if anything could outrun destiny, the eye would.”

24
00:01:46,970 --> 00:01:54,160
And in the house of Umm Salama he saw a girl with a safʿa on her face, a change in her colour,

25
00:01:54,250 --> 00:01:57,570
and said: “Seek ruqyah for her, for she has been struck by the eye.”

26
00:01:57,660 --> 00:02:03,750
A child is lovely; eyes cling to him, he is praised, and phones pass his picture around,

27
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:07,450
while he cannot mention Allah over himself or protect himself.

28
00:02:07,540 --> 00:02:10,420
So protecting him is a trust upon the parents’ necks.

29
00:02:10,510 --> 00:02:12,370
Signs that those who practise ruqyah mention

30
00:02:12,460 --> 00:02:19,300
Experienced practitioners mention signs that usually appear suddenly, after a visit, a compliment or a glance:

31
00:02:19,390 --> 00:02:21,930
long crying with no apparent cause,

32
00:02:22,020 --> 00:02:23,870
sleeplessness night and day,

33
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:25,650
refusing to feed,

34
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:28,290
restlessness even in his mother’s arms,

35
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:30,290
and sudden fright from sleep.

36
00:02:30,380 --> 00:02:33,250
Yet these signs are not conclusive,

37
00:02:33,340 --> 00:02:35,060
for not every cry is the eye,

38
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:39,300
so we do not blame everything on the eye, nor accuse anyone without proof.

39
00:02:39,390 --> 00:02:49,130
The beauty of sharʿī ruqyah is that if it is the eye, then by Allah’s leave it is a cure, and if not, it is remembrance, prayer and blessing, with no harm in it.

40
00:02:49,220 --> 00:02:52,130
And now, the treatment, step by step.

41
00:02:52,220 --> 00:02:55,060
Step one: certainty and reliance on Allah.

42
00:02:55,150 --> 00:03:00,570
Allah says: “And We send down of the Qur’an that which is healing and mercy for the believers.”

43
00:03:00,660 --> 00:03:06,720
Recite while certain that the Healer is Allah alone, not you and not your words.

44
00:03:07,570 --> 00:03:10,720
Step two: reciting over the child.

45
00:03:10,810 --> 00:03:18,120
ʿĀʾisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reported that when the Prophet (peace be upon him) fell ill, he would recite the Muʿawwidhāt over himself and blow lightly.

46
00:03:18,210 --> 00:03:21,610
Sit near your child in a state of wudūʾ,

47
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:24,890
place your right hand gently on his head or chest,

48
00:03:24,980 --> 00:03:28,840
and recite, blowing lightly over him after each sura.

49
00:03:28,930 --> 00:03:30,540
Every morning and evening:

50
00:03:30,630 --> 00:03:35,590
Al-Fātiḥa seven times, Āyat al-Kursī, and the last verses of Sūrat al-Baqara, “The Messenger believes”,

51
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:40,150
and al-Ikhlāṣ, al-Falaq and an-Nās, three times each.

52
00:03:40,650 --> 00:03:48,840
As for al-Fātiḥa, a Companion recited it over a sick man and he recovered, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) said to him: “How did you know it is a ruqyah?”

53
00:03:48,940 --> 00:03:53,470
The number seven comes from the experience of practitioners; what matters is a present heart.

54
00:03:53,560 --> 00:04:00,720
Āyat al-Kursī: “Whoever recites it will have a guardian from Allah over him, and no devil will come near him until morning.”

55
00:04:00,810 --> 00:04:04,640
The end of al-Baqara: “Whoever recites the two in a night, they will suffice him.”

56
00:04:04,730 --> 00:04:13,030
Of the Muʿawwidhāt he (peace be upon him) said: “Recite them when you reach evening and when you reach morning, three times; they will suffice you against everything.”

57
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:17,220
Step three: the supplications of the Prophet (peace be upon him).

58
00:04:17,310 --> 00:04:26,680
He used to seek refuge for al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn with the words: “I seek refuge for you in the perfect words of Allah from every devil and every harmful creature, and from every evil eye.”

59
00:04:26,770 --> 00:04:34,060
So say to your child: “I seek refuge for you in the perfect words of Allah from every devil and every harmful creature, and from every evil eye.”

60
00:04:34,140 --> 00:04:43,980
Jibrīl (peace be upon him) performed ruqyah for the Prophet (peace be upon him), saying: “In the name of Allah I perform ruqyah for you, from everything that harms you, from the evil of every soul or envious eye,

61
00:04:44,070 --> 00:04:47,230
may Allah heal you; in the name of Allah I perform ruqyah for you.”

62
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:48,040
And pray:

63
00:04:48,130 --> 00:04:56,860
“O Allah, Lord of mankind, remove the harm; heal him, for You are the Healer; there is no healing but Your healing, a healing that leaves no illness behind.”

64
00:04:56,950 --> 00:05:02,210
And say seven times: “I ask Allah the Almighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to heal you.”

65
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:05,020
Step four: the water of ruqyah.

66
00:05:05,110 --> 00:05:09,630
Recite these suras and supplications over a vessel of water, and blow lightly into it.

67
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:12,640
If the child is older, he drinks from it,

68
00:05:12,730 --> 00:05:16,920
and if he is an infant, wipe his face, hands and feet with the water,

69
00:05:17,010 --> 00:05:19,730
and many scholars have permitted this.

70
00:05:19,820 --> 00:05:22,960
Step five: the parents’ istighfar.

71
00:05:23,050 --> 00:05:29,140
Seek your Lord’s forgiveness, for there may be a cause we do not know, and istighfar may become a cause of healing.

72
00:05:29,230 --> 00:05:41,440
Allah says on the tongue of Nūḥ (peace be upon him): “I said: seek forgiveness of your Lord, He is ever Forgiving; He will send rain upon you in abundance, and support you with wealth and children.”

73
00:05:41,530 --> 00:05:44,980
Reflect how Allah linked istighfar with blessing in children.

74
00:05:45,070 --> 00:05:52,390
So make much of it, dear mother, as you do housework, on the road, and beside your little one’s cradle, and pray for him with a broken heart.

75
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:55,520
Step six: the washing of the one who cast the eye

76
00:05:55,610 --> 00:06:04,170
Sahl ibn Ḥunayf was struck by the eye and collapsed, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) said to the one who struck him: “Why does one of you kill his brother? Why did you not invoke blessing?”

77
00:06:04,260 --> 00:06:07,720
And he ordered him to wash for him, and Sahl got up, healed.

78
00:06:07,810 --> 00:06:11,610
And he (peace be upon him) said: “If you are asked to wash, then wash.”

79
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:14,650
But this is only where there is certainty, not suspicion or guesswork,

80
00:06:14,740 --> 00:06:17,310
and it is requested gently, without dispute.

81
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:20,540
Step seven: patience and persistence.

82
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:25,920
Ruqyah is not the work of a single day; keep at it for days and weeks and do not despair,

83
00:06:26,010 --> 00:06:28,930
for healing comes at the time Allah wills.

84
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:30,520
And beware of charlatans.

85
00:06:30,610 --> 00:06:38,370
He (peace be upon him) said: “There is no harm in ruqyah as long as it contains no shirk,” and said: “Whoever hangs an amulet has committed shirk.”

86
00:06:38,460 --> 00:06:49,410
If someone writes a talisman for your child, hands you a paper of unintelligible words, asks for your mother’s name, or asks you to slaughter an animal, know that this is not the way of the sharīʿa.

87
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:57,230
Sharʿī ruqyah is Qur’an and prophetic supplications, in clear words you understand, and you and his father are the people most entitled to recite it over him.

88
00:06:57,320 --> 00:07:01,350
And remember his saying (peace be upon him): “Seek treatment, servants of Allah.”

89
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:04,780
Ruqyah does not cancel taking the means; it supports them,

90
00:07:04,870 --> 00:07:07,450
and prevention is better than waiting for affliction.

91
00:07:07,540 --> 00:07:13,820
If something about a child impresses you, say: “What Allah wills, there is no power but with Allah,” or: “May Allah bless him.”

92
00:07:13,910 --> 00:07:19,830
Allah says: “If only, when you entered your garden, you had said: What Allah wills; there is no power but with Allah.”

93
00:07:19,920 --> 00:07:25,800
And he (peace be upon him) said: “If one of you sees something he admires in his brother, let him invoke blessing for him.”

94
00:07:25,890 --> 00:07:33,190
And share fewer of your child’s pictures and private moments on social media, for not every glance comes with a prayer.

95
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:38,880
Protect him morning and evening with the Prophet’s protective words (peace be upon him), and say three times:

96
00:07:38,970 --> 00:07:44,070
“In the name of Allah, with whose name nothing on earth or in heaven can cause harm, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.”

97
00:07:44,160 --> 00:07:51,570
And fill your home with Qur’an, for he (peace be upon him) told us that the devil flees from a house in which Sūrat al-Baqara is recited.

98
00:07:51,660 --> 00:07:55,970
In short: the eye is real, but Allah is greater than every glance,

99
00:07:56,060 --> 00:07:59,200
the Qur’an is healing, but the Healer is Allah,

100
00:07:59,290 --> 00:08:03,320
and the parents are the first to recite ruqyah over the child and the people most entitled to do so.

101
00:08:03,410 --> 00:08:12,870
If you know a mother who stays up nights beside her little one’s cradle, send her this clip, and write in the comments a prayer for every sick child.

102
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:17,080
“O Allah, heal our children and the children of the Muslims, and clothe them in the garment of well-being.”

103
00:08:17,170 --> 00:08:17,980
Amen.

